## SQ-RING-01
@group A
@commands Boot a new world; grep latest.log for `[rings]` and `Mixin`; then `/locate structure minecraft:stronghold` and note the result
@pass One `not stored ... computing` and one `stored in the world's data` line per ring set (vanilla strongholds, Better Strongholds); `world/data/creativeengineering_ring_positions.json` exists with 128 x,z pairs per set
@fails No `[rings]` line: the mixin did not apply (check `m_223148_`); `no cache key` warning: read the stack trace (codec encode or probe)
@reviewed 2026-11-16
bootexpect \[rings\] .*not stored for this world and pack, computing
bootexpect \[rings\] .*positions stored in the world's data
bootreject \[rings\] .*(could not store|unreadable)
bootreject (?i)Mixin apply failed.*[Rr]ing
shell grep -n "\[rings\]\|Preparing spawn area" logs/latest.log | head -8 | cut -c1-200
shell python3 -c "import json,sys; d=json.load(open(sys.argv[1])); print({k: (len(v) if isinstance(v,list) else type(v).__name__) for k,v in (d.items() if isinstance(d,dict) else [])})" world/data/creativeengineering_ring_positions.json
> locate structure minecraft:stronghold
waitlog (nearest minecraft:stronghold|Could not find) 300
capture RG is at \[(-?\d+), (~|-?\d+), (-?\d+)\]
look one computing and one stored line per ring set (vanilla, Better Strongholds); the json shape shows 128 pairs per set; note the stronghold position for SQ-RING-02
## SQ-RING-02
@group A
@commands `/stop`, boot again; grep `[rings]`; repeat the `/locate` from SQ-RING-01; time "Preparing spawn area" against SQ-RING-01's boot
@pass `positions from the world's data` per set, key time well under 1 s; the same locate result; the level-creation stretch about 12 s shorter
@fails `computing` again: the key is not stable between boots (an input is non-deterministic; diff the keys in the file)
@reviewed 2026-11-16
bootexpect \[rings\] .*positions from the world's data
bootreject \[rings\] .*computing
shell grep -n "\[rings\]\|Preparing spawn area" logs/latest.log | head -8 | cut -c1-200
> locate structure minecraft:stronghold
waitlog (nearest minecraft:stronghold|Could not find) 300
waitlog is at \[{RG1}, (~|-?\d+), {RG3}\] 10
look the key time well under 1 s; the level-creation stretch about 12 s shorter than SQ-RING-01's boot (restart of the same world)
## SQ-RING-03
@group A
@commands `/stop`; change the seed in `server.properties` and delete `world/`, or add a datapack biome change to the same world; boot
@pass `computing` again with a new key; the new positions are stored next to the old entry
@fails Old positions reused: the key misses the changed input
@reviewed 2026-11-16
bootexpect \[rings\] .*not stored for this world and pack, computing
bootexpect \[rings\] .*positions stored in the world's data
shell grep -c '"' world/data/creativeengineering_ring_positions.json; true
look own boot after a seed change with world/ deleted, or a datapack biome change on the same world: computing with a new key; on the same world the file holds the old entry beside the new one
